# LaTeX build artifacts
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
*.synctex.gz
*.bbl
*.blg

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Matplotlib / font / OS caches
.cache/
.mplconfig/
.DS_Store

# Large binaries (compiled paper PDFs are tracked deliverables, not ignored)
*.mp4

# Vendored third-party assets (mujoco_menagerie model zoo, >1 GB of meshes)
external_deps/

# Vendored mesh assets and regenerable simulation logs
*.stl
*.STL
*.npz

# Generated terrain/torque MJCF variants written into results/ by the
# benchmarks. Regenerable, and they embed an absolute machine-local
# meshdir, so they must not be committed.
**/results/g1_wbc_torque_*.xml

# EXCEPTION: v5's G1 meshes ARE tracked. They are the 12-DoF legs-only G1 from
# unitree_rl_gym, and three of the 27 (torso_link_23dof_rev_1_0.STL and the two
# *_wrist_roll_rubber_hand.STL) have no mujoco_menagerie equivalent -- those
# three are also the largest, 14.8 of the 25.2 MB -- so no auto-fetch fallback
# can reconstruct this set. Committing them is the only way v5 reproduces from
# a clean checkout. v3/v4 meshes stay ignored: robot_descriptions supplies them.
!versions/v5/code/g1_description/meshes/*.STL

# EXCEPTION: v3 is archived (superseded by v4), so its irreplaceable outputs are
# tracked rather than left one `rm` away from permanent loss. The rendered demo
# videos cannot be cheaply regenerated, and the built PDFs are the archived
# record. Deliberately NOT tracked for v3: the 51 STL meshes (robot_descriptions
# supplies them since 2251856), the 28 MB of per-seed *.npz trial logs (a single
# regenerable condition), and generated/cache files.
!versions/v3/videos/*.mp4

# NOTE: compiled paper PDFs are tracked deliverables (the blanket *.pdf rule was
# removed on main). This matters for v5 specifically: wbc_v5.tex writes
# \includegraphics{name} with no extension, so LaTeX prefers the .pdf figure
# over the .png of the same basename -- versions/v5/code/figures/*.pdf must stay
# tracked or a clone silently builds against the raster fallbacks.

# XeLaTeX intermediate (produced when building the _zh papers)
*.xdv

# Downloaded third-party reference papers and superseded draft builds. Removing
# the blanket *.pdf rule (so compiled deliverables are tracked) exposed these as
# untracked noise; they are inputs and history, not deliverables.
/[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9].[0-9]*.pdf
/centroidal_double_integrator.pdf
/g1_simulation_design.pdf
/wbc_rewrite.pdf
versions/v0_original/**/*.pdf
versions/v1_honest/**/*.pdf
